syrinx@stein.u.washington.edu (Syrinx) writes:

>Also, Dev Team:  It sure would be nice if there were also a stat given for
>how much weight your character is currently carrying (the same way it
>shows how many hit points you have left).

Probably not the best way to implement it, since humans (and elves?) aren't
really THAT good at measuring weight "by-eye".  Best would be a simple command
that allows you to pick up two items, and see their COMPARTIVE weights:

	#weigh
	In you left claw: [a-zA-X]? a
	In you right claw: [a-zA-X]? b
	The hawaiian shirt welds to your hand!
	The mithril coat is slightly heavier than the hawaiian shirt.

	#weigh
	In you left claw: [a-zA-X]? c
	[The hawaiian shirt in your right hand is cursed]
	The leather jacket is slightly heavier than the hawaiian shirt.

	The ant bites!
	You begin bashing monsters with a cursed -2 hawaiian shirt.
	... You die.

This brings up another point: why can't we fight left-handed when that 
shirt has tied itself to our right-hand?

Of course Cavemen are 50% left-handed, Knights are 100% right-handed,
and wizards are ambidextrous (but weak anyway).  [of course, let the
options override any fascist dictum of race tendancies...]

